Subject: [PATCH 27/36] Finder column view: path highlight, tidy preview; real
 folders stay folders

- The current item and the folders leading to it are always highlighted
  (blue in the active column, gray before it), even when selection and
  focus are elsewhere.
- Preview: long names wrap over up to three lines (anywhere if they have
  no spaces), Finder dates ("Today at 1:30 PM"), decimal sizes, a
  see-through background, and real thumbnails where KDE can make them.
- Undo treating folders whose names look like disk images (e.g. *.iso) as
  files in Recents: they are real folders.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01KdkdNUmoM62iDwjRop6X5f
